      "writtenOn": "2026-07-29T07:57:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not exactly. For example, look at https://review.gerrithub.io/c/davidsaOpenu/simulator/+/1237496/21/infra/builder/load_config.sh#b95 where you removed the extraction of EVSSIM_GUEST_TESTS_GUEST_VM_IMAGE from the JSON file and overrode it with the default VERSION_QEMU_IMAGE\u003d\"${EVSSIM_GUEST_TESTS_GUEST_VM_IMAGE#ubuntu:}\". In fact, anyone who removes lines from load_config and then sets default values creates a headache where the values are coming from. This approach leads to long and time-consuming debugging in case of missing values (running the code looking for container tags, etc.). That\u0027s why the JSON file has to be the only source of truth for versions.",
      "parentUuid": "de4dcd1d_536c996b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 56,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "702600e4ab98a1bca932853292e0c81b55a2a815",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "91996cac_7a650cde",
        "filename": "infra/builder/run-ci.sh",
        "patchSetId": 21
      },
      "lineNbr": 21,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039371
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-30T11:04:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "First of all, I did not remove `EVSSIM_GUEST_TESTS_GUEST_VM_IMAGE` and overrode it with a default.\nI removed the `extract` from `load_config.sh` because that was from the part that reads the **links** from the JSON, the links are removed *as was discussed*.\nInstead there is now a JSON variable called `guestVmImage` which holds a string(instead of a link) of the version. You can see in the same change a few lines prior, where it is loaded, so the `EVSSIM_GUEST_TESTS_GUEST_VM_IMAGE` still exists and is still loaded.\n\nSecond of all, there is no default overriding anything. The JSON is still the only source of truth. The `#` removes a prefix from a string, default values are set with `-`, not a `#`. The `#` is needed because the values in the JSON are `ubuntu:26.04` and `ubuntu:14.04`, so the `#ubuntu:` removes the `ubuntu:` part. I would much prefer if the values in the JSON were something `26.04` and `14.04` (or even better, `u14.04`/`u26.04` or `ubuntu26.04`/`ubuntu14.04`, or similar, and same for the docker image names, and then if the base distro for the system switches again, as it has in the past from centos or whatever else has been, nothing in the code needs to be changed, the new values and Dockerfies will just be under the name, for example, `alma10`, instead of having to rewrite all the `ubuntu:` assumptions), the same as the docker image names and then this hardcoded prefix removal would not be needed.",
      "parentUuid": "a9e3672f_76589a80",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 56,
        "endLine": 21,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "702600e4ab98a1bca932853292e0c81b55a2a815",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
